error[RB0323]: `Nested<T[]>` refers back to `Nested` with other type arguments than its parameters `<T>`
 --> RB0323-irregular-recursion.road:1:25
  |
1 | type Nested<T> { inner: Nested<T[]>? }
  |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^
  |
  = help: a generic type can refer to itself, directly or through other types, only with its own parameters, in order, so that it has finitely many instances

